<title>NETHERLANDS: SGS Europe cocoa stock estimates up at end-Jan.</title>
<headline>SGS Europe cocoa stock estimates up at end-Jan.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>SGS Warehouse Services gave the following estimates of cocoa beans in store in Europe as of the end of January/early February. All figures in tonnes.</p>
<p>		     Total	     Of which for the buffer stock</p>
<p>AMSTERDAM	  516,000	   35,034 (incl   990 forw. sales)</p>
<p>HAMBURG/BREMEN   122,000	   15,512</p>
<p>ANTWERP	     86,250	    2,032 (incl 1,450 forw sales)</p>
<p>UK (ALL PORTS)    52,375	    3,785 (incl 3,785 forw sales)</p>
<p>ROTTERDAM	   13,000	    9,429 (incl    75 forw sales)</p>
<p>The data gives the following changes to month-earlier levels:</p>
<p>AMSTERDAM	  UP  48,000 HAMBURG/BREMEN   UP  11,250</p>
<p>ANTWERP	    UP   1,250 UK (ALL PORTS)   UP   4,875</p>
<p>ROTTERDAM	  NO CHANGE</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
